WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.931 --> 00:05.202 align:center line:79%
When commanded to choose the new King
of Israel from among the sons of Jesse,

00:05.502 --> 00:08.405 align:center line:79%
the prophet Samuel,
upon looking at Jesse's oldest son,

00:08.405 --> 00:14.144 align:center line:79%
Eliab, exclaimed with enthusiasm,
“Surely the Lord’s anointed is before

00:14.645 --> 00:17.381 align:center line:79%
him.” But Eliab was not
the Lord’s chosen servant.

00:17.781 --> 00:19.316 align:center line:81%
The Savior warned Samuel:

00:19.616 --> 00:23.086 align:center line:79%
“Look not on his countenance
or on the height of his stature;

00:23.287 --> 00:25.889 align:center line:81%
because I have refused him: For the Lord

00:25.923 --> 00:27.324 align:center line:81%
Seeth not as man seeth;

00:27.624 --> 00:33.063 align:center line:79%
for man looketh on the outward appearance,
but the Lord looketh on the heart.”

00:33.630 --> 00:37.267 align:center line:79%
While David may have not been
physically the strongest

00:37.267 --> 00:41.471 align:center line:79%
or most skilled of his brothers,
his heart was strong in the sight of God.

00:41.872 --> 00:46.143 align:center line:79%
He loved God with all his heart
and had a deep desire to obey him.

00:46.810 --> 00:51.214 align:center line:79%
He had unwavering faith in God’s love,
power, and promised blessings,

00:51.214 --> 00:53.951 align:center line:79%
as he later demonstrated
when he fearlessly fought

00:53.951 --> 00:56.253 align:center line:81%
and defeated Goliath with the Lord's help.

00:56.853 --> 01:01.024 align:center line:79%
This story teaches us that all
God needs to accomplish His purposes

01:01.191 --> 01:03.894 align:center line:79%
and to help us become
who He wants us to become

01:04.194 --> 01:07.464 align:center line:79%
is for each of us
to turn our hearts fully to Him.

01:07.998 --> 01:12.836 align:center line:79%
To a lawyer He commanded, “Thou shalt
love the Lord thy God with all thy heart.”

01:13.236 --> 01:16.073 align:center line:79%
To the Prophet Joseph Smith
He said, “Behold,

01:16.073 --> 01:18.709 align:center line:79%
the Lord requireth the heart
and a willing mind.”

01:19.076 --> 01:23.046 align:center line:79%
And to the Nephites, the resurrected
Savior extended this invitation:

01:23.447 --> 01:28.018 align:center line:79%
“Ye shall offer for a sacrifice unto me
a broken heart and a contrite spirit.”

01:28.652 --> 01:33.323 align:center line:79%
Why is that so? The Savior taught that
if our hearts are fully turned to Him,

01:33.590 --> 01:35.626 align:center line:81%
because of His atoning sacrifice

01:35.659 --> 01:37.394 align:center line:81%
we can be blessed with the strength

01:37.394 --> 01:41.164 align:center line:79%
and spiritual gifts we need
to overcome our mortal challenges,

01:41.331 --> 01:44.901 align:center line:79%
resist temptation,
receive direction and understanding,

01:44.901 --> 01:47.404 align:center line:81%
and feel joy and peace in our lives.

01:47.871 --> 01:51.108 align:center line:79%
“Out of small things proceedeth
that which is great,” He said

01:51.541 --> 01:54.044 align:center line:81%
He can make “weak things become strong”

01:54.244 --> 01:58.215 align:center line:79%
and bless us with everything we need
to succeed in this mortal life

01:58.348 --> 02:00.083 align:center line:81%
and to receive eternal life.

02:00.550 --> 02:04.354 align:center line:79%
“Blessed are the pure in heart,”
He said, “for they shall see God.”

02:05.088 --> 02:07.591 align:center line:81%
I believe this is why, at least in part,

02:07.691 --> 02:10.193 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ so often
corrected the scribes

02:10.193 --> 02:12.262 align:center line:81%
and Pharisees during His mortal ministry.

02:12.763 --> 02:17.034 align:center line:79%
Though diligent in keeping His law,
they did so for the wrong reasons.

02:17.467 --> 02:22.005 align:center line:79%
He rebuked them, saying, “This people
draweth nigh unto me with their mouth,

02:22.005 --> 02:25.676 align:center line:79%
and honoureth me with their lips;
but their heart is far from me.”

02:26.543 --> 02:28.011 align:center line:81%
This is a sober reminder

02:28.011 --> 02:31.782 align:center line:79%
to all His disciples that it is not
just about what we do—

02:32.049 --> 02:37.120 align:center line:79%
our words and actions—but also why we do
what Jesus Christ has asked us to do—

02:37.287 --> 02:39.156 align:center line:81%
our desires and motives.

02:39.723 --> 02:44.561 align:center line:79%
He said, “For I, the Lord, will judge
all men according to their works,

02:44.728 --> 02:46.763 align:center line:81%
according to the desire of their hearts.”

02:47.431 --> 02:50.867 align:center line:79%
Our Heavenly Father desires more
than mechanical acts of obedience

02:50.867 --> 02:52.436 align:center line:81%
and service from His children.

02:52.836 --> 02:55.639 align:center line:79%
He wants us to do those things
with real intent

02:55.806 --> 02:57.908 align:center line:81%
because we love Him with all our hearts.

02:58.241 --> 03:00.844 align:center line:81%
He wants us to desire to become like Him.

03:01.812 --> 03:05.982 align:center line:79%
Now, if the spiritual health of our hearts
is a main concern of the Savior—

03:06.249 --> 03:08.251 align:center line:81%
what He looks for in a true disciple—

03:08.585 --> 03:12.789 align:center line:79%
how can we examine our hearts and know
if it is right in the sight of God?

03:13.523 --> 03:17.360 align:center line:79%
Recently, as my wife and I
returned from our mission in Portugal,

03:17.694 --> 03:21.465 align:center line:79%
we ran a series of health tests
to evaluate our physical condition.

03:21.898 --> 03:25.669 align:center line:79%
Some of those tests focused
on our heart health, such as blood tests,

03:25.702 --> 03:27.904 align:center line:81%
echocardiograms, and stress tests.

03:28.371 --> 03:32.042 align:center line:79%
I believe the Savior has also
provided us with a set

03:32.042 --> 03:36.713 align:center line:79%
of spiritual tests we can use to assess
our heart's spiritual condition.

03:37.214 --> 03:38.749 align:center line:81%
Let me share a few with you.

03:39.382 --> 03:45.188 align:center line:79%
First, our focus, priorities,
and motives. “For where your treasure is,

03:45.188 --> 03:46.723 align:center line:81%
there will your heart be also,”

03:46.723 --> 03:50.260 align:center line:79%
Jesus taught. A treasure is
something precious to us,

03:50.260 --> 03:53.063 align:center line:79%
something to which we dedicate
effort and attention.

03:53.563 --> 03:57.434 align:center line:79%
Where we choose to spend
our time and focus our attention,

03:57.434 --> 04:02.105 align:center line:79%
as well as what motivates us to do
what we do, says a lot about our hearts.

04:02.839 --> 04:06.109 align:center line:79%
The Savior warned that while
many are called by Him,

04:06.176 --> 04:08.712 align:center line:79%
few are chosen
“because their hearts are set

04:08.712 --> 04:13.283 align:center line:79%
so much upon the things of this world,
and [they] aspire to the honors of men.”

04:14.184 --> 04:17.454 align:center line:79%
Do I make the Savior
a priority in my life?

04:18.121 --> 04:21.892 align:center line:79%
Is my eye single
to His glory in all that I do?

04:22.793 --> 04:26.163 align:center line:79%
Second, our willingness
to obey God's commandments.

04:26.596 --> 04:27.798 align:center line:81%
Throughout scripture,

04:27.964 --> 04:31.501 align:center line:79%
the Lord and His prophets have associated
pride and disobedience

04:31.501 --> 04:33.170 align:center line:81%
with having a hardened heart.

04:33.770 --> 04:36.473 align:center line:81%
Nephi exhorted his brothers, saying,

04:36.740 --> 04:40.243 align:center line:79%
“How is it that you do not keep
the commandments of the Lord?

04:40.243 --> 04:44.414 align:center line:79%
How is it that you will perish because
of the hardness of your hearts?”

04:44.414 --> 04:46.650 align:center line:81%
To the Saints in Missouri the Lord warned,

04:46.850 --> 04:50.353 align:center line:79%
“But he that doeth not
anything until he is commanded,

04:50.353 --> 04:53.223 align:center line:79%
and receiveth a commandment
with a doubtful heart,

04:53.223 --> 04:56.193 align:center line:79%
and keepeth it with slothfulness,
the same is damned.”

04:56.760 --> 05:00.597 align:center line:79%
While the Savior does not expect
perfection in keeping His commandments,

05:00.864 --> 05:05.135 align:center line:79%
He does ask that we desire and strive
to keep them with all our hearts.

05:06.036 --> 05:10.340 align:center line:79%
Third, our diligence in studying
the scriptures and seeking revelation.

05:10.974 --> 05:15.345 align:center line:79%
The Lord admonished Oliver Cowdery
to “treasure up these words in thy heart.”

05:15.679 --> 05:18.682 align:center line:79%
We're invited to search
the scriptures diligently

05:18.682 --> 05:22.519 align:center line:79%
and through the power of the Holy Ghost,
seek to obtain understanding

05:22.519 --> 05:26.223 align:center line:79%
and a witness of the truthfulness
of the gospel in our hearts.

05:26.923 --> 05:30.260 align:center line:79%
The prophet Abinadi rebuked
the priests of the wicked King Noah

05:30.260 --> 05:34.698 align:center line:79%
for not doing that, saying,“Ye have not
applied your hearts to understanding;

05:34.965 --> 05:37.133 align:center line:81%
therefore, ye have not been wise.”

05:38.001 --> 05:41.671 align:center line:79%
Am I making a sincere effort
to study the scriptures daily

05:41.838 --> 05:44.941 align:center line:79%
and to apply my heart
to understand them through prayer?

05:46.042 --> 05:48.745 align:center line:81%
Fourth, our thoughts and words.

05:49.279 --> 05:52.749 align:center line:79%
The Savior taught that “out
of the heart proceeded evil thoughts,”

05:52.749 --> 05:56.453 align:center line:79%
and that “out of the abundance
of the heart the mouth speaketh.”

05:56.453 --> 05:57.821 align:center line:81%
The quality of our thoughts

05:57.821 --> 06:01.324 align:center line:79%
and words is a good indicator
of the purity of our hearts.

06:01.958 --> 06:05.662 align:center line:79%
Am I fostering too many negative
thoughts about others’ actions or motives,

06:05.662 --> 06:07.230 align:center line:81%
or even about myself?

06:07.898 --> 06:10.734 align:center line:79%
Am I too quick to judge
and condemn others?

06:11.301 --> 06:15.572 align:center line:79%
Do I seek to find excuses
or justification for my mistakes?

06:16.006 --> 06:17.474 align:center line:81%
And what about my words?

06:17.941 --> 06:20.343 align:center line:81%
Do they lift and inspire those around me?

06:20.577 --> 06:24.047 align:center line:79%
Or do they often create
conflict and resentment?

06:24.047 --> 06:25.982 align:center line:81%
After my physical tests were completed,

06:25.982 --> 06:29.586 align:center line:79%
my doctor told me that overall
my heart was healthy,

06:29.886 --> 06:32.822 align:center line:79%
but there were a few concerns
that needed to be addressed now,

06:32.822 --> 06:34.491 align:center line:81%
before they became serious.

06:34.991 --> 06:37.494 align:center line:81%
He then prescribed some lifestyle changes.

06:38.194 --> 06:41.831 align:center line:79%
Likewise, as you perform the spiritual
assessment of your heart

06:41.831 --> 06:46.336 align:center line:79%
and notice some negative symptoms starting
to creep in, please don't panic.

06:46.937 --> 06:50.206 align:center line:79%
The Savior has provided
excellent spiritual medication

06:50.206 --> 06:51.608 align:center line:81%
and treatment to help you.

06:52.108 --> 06:54.844 align:center line:79%
He has even promised
to give you a new heart.

06:55.578 --> 06:59.349 align:center line:79%
Here are some actions that can improve
your heart's spiritual strength.

06:59.816 --> 07:02.585 align:center line:81%
First, your relationship with Christ.

07:02.953 --> 07:07.724 align:center line:79%
As we dedicate time daily to come closer
to Christ, our hearts are changed.

07:08.258 --> 07:09.960 align:center line:81%
Daily study of the scriptures,

07:09.960 --> 07:13.363 align:center line:79%
accompanied by sincere
prayer and regular fasting,

07:13.396 --> 07:16.933 align:center line:79%
will increase your love for the Savior
and strengthen your faith

07:16.933 --> 07:20.470 align:center line:79%
and desire to repent and humbly
yield your heart to God.

07:21.237 --> 07:23.173 align:center line:81%
Consider this example from Nephi:

07:23.707 --> 07:27.844 align:center line:79%
“Wherefore, I did cry unto the Lord;
and behold, he did visit me,

07:28.078 --> 07:31.348 align:center line:79%
and did soften my heart
that I did believe all the words

07:31.348 --> 07:33.283 align:center line:81%
which had been spoken by my father.”

07:33.950 --> 07:37.754 align:center line:79%
As we continue to nourish the seed
of faith by our righteous desires

07:37.754 --> 07:41.558 align:center line:79%
and actions, we will experience
the same sanctification

07:41.558 --> 07:43.093 align:center line:81%
of our hearts as the Nephites:

07:43.727 --> 07:45.462 align:center line:81%
“They did fast and pray oft,

07:45.462 --> 07:48.398 align:center line:79%
and did wax stronger and stronger
in their humility,

07:48.398 --> 07:51.067 align:center line:79%
and firmer and firmer
in the faith of Christ,

07:51.267 --> 07:55.205 align:center line:79%
unto the filling their souls
with joy and consolation, yea,

07:55.605 --> 07:59.042 align:center line:79%
even to the purifying
and the sanctification of their hearts,

07:59.275 --> 08:03.446 align:center line:79%
which sanctification cometh because
of their yielding their hearts unto God.”

08:04.547 --> 08:06.750 align:center line:81%
Second, align your will with His.

08:07.183 --> 08:10.954 align:center line:79%
The Savior taught, “If ye love me,
keep my commandments.”

08:11.287 --> 08:15.525 align:center line:79%
He invites us to demonstrate our love
by making and keeping covenants with Him.

08:15.525 --> 08:17.694 align:center line:79%
As we strive daily to
keep His commandments,

08:17.694 --> 08:19.829 align:center line:81%
sincerely repent from our sins,

08:19.829 --> 08:23.933 align:center line:79%
and persevere in taking His name upon
us and aligning our will with His will,

08:24.167 --> 08:28.071 align:center line:79%
we can be blessed with the constant
companionship of the Holy Ghost.

08:28.071 --> 08:32.308 align:center line:79%
Nephi testified, “I know that if ye
shall follow the Son, with full purpose

08:32.308 --> 08:35.979 align:center line:79%
of heart, acting no hypocrisy
and no deception before God,

08:35.979 --> 08:39.082 align:center line:79%
but with real intent,
repenting of your sins,

08:39.149 --> 08:41.818 align:center line:79%
witnessing unto the Father
that ye are willing to take upon

08:41.818 --> 08:46.122 align:center line:79%
you the name of Christ by baptism ...
then ye shall receive the Holy Ghost.”

08:46.589 --> 08:48.024 align:center line:81%
The Holy Ghost will guide you

08:48.024 --> 08:51.528 align:center line:79%
and help you know the will of the Lord
and make good choices.

08:51.528 --> 08:54.330 align:center line:79%
Last, serve God and others
with all your heart.

08:54.664 --> 08:58.134 align:center line:79%
The Savior invites all
to “serve him with all your heart.”

08:58.134 --> 09:01.371 align:center line:79%
When we choose to do each
thing the Lord has asked us to do—

09:01.371 --> 09:04.574 align:center line:79%
such as keeping the commandments,
partaking of the sacrament,

09:04.574 --> 09:08.344 align:center line:79%
worshiping in the temple, and serving
others—with a sincere heart

09:08.344 --> 09:09.479 align:center line:81%
and with real intent,

09:09.779 --> 09:13.216 align:center line:79%
each act of service and worship
becomes a powerful spiritual

09:13.216 --> 09:16.619 align:center line:79%
experience that strengthens
our faith and testimony,

09:16.619 --> 09:20.523 align:center line:79%
and fill our hearts with joy and love
for God and our fellow man.

09:20.523 --> 09:23.960 align:center line:79%
The prophet Alma’s question
still echoes today: “Have ye

09:23.993 --> 09:25.728 align:center line:81%
spiritually been born of God?

09:26.262 --> 09:29.132 align:center line:79%
Have ye received his image
in your countenances?

09:29.132 --> 09:32.569 align:center line:79%
Have ye experienced this mighty
change in your hearts?”

09:33.203 --> 09:34.370 align:center line:81%
Brothers and sisters,

09:34.704 --> 09:37.807 align:center line:79%
I invite you to give your whole heart
to the Savior today.

09:38.475 --> 09:42.779 align:center line:79%
Let each act of worship
and service be sincere and intentional.

09:43.279 --> 09:45.715 align:center line:81%
Set aside the distractions of the world

09:45.715 --> 09:49.686 align:center line:79%
and strive to have meaningful time
for the Lord every day of your lives.

09:50.086 --> 09:53.423 align:center line:79%
Repent and return
to Him with all your heart,

09:53.423 --> 09:56.993 align:center line:79%
and He will forgive you and encircle you
in the arms of His love.

09:57.527 --> 09:59.596 align:center line:81%
Seek not the things of this world,

09:59.596 --> 10:02.165 align:center line:79%
but choose to have your eye
single to His glory,

10:02.165 --> 10:04.067 align:center line:81%
and seek the things of a better one.

10:04.534 --> 10:08.738 align:center line:79%
He knows your thoughts and the desires
of your heart. And as you come unto Him,

10:08.738 --> 10:13.109 align:center line:79%
He will bless you with strength,
confidence, peace, and joy

10:13.243 --> 10:17.514 align:center line:79%
in this life and a place
in His celestial kingdom for all eternity.

10:17.514 --> 10:19.349 align:center line:81%
I know Jesus Christ lives.

10:19.482 --> 10:24.220 align:center line:79%
He is our Redeemer, and He loves
you and I with all His heart.

10:24.420 --> 10:26.723 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

